{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cctype>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include <map>\n#include <set>\n#include <queue>\n#include <stack>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <numeric>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\ni64 digitCount(i64 val) {\n    if (val == 0) return 1;\n    if (val < 0) val = -val;\n    i64 cnt = 0;\n    while (val > 0) {\n        ++cnt;\n        val /= 10;\n    }\n    return cnt;\n}\n\ni64 incrementEachDigit(i64 val) {\n    vector<int> digits;\n    bool isNegative = val < 0;\n    if (isNegative) val = -val;\n    while (val > 0) {\n        int d = val % 10;\n        digits.push_back(d - (isNegative ? -1 : 1));\n        val /= 10;\n    }\n    i64 res = 0;\n    for (int i = digits.size() - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        res = res * 10 + digits[i];\n    }\n    return isNegative ? -res : res;\n}\n\ni64 decrementEachDigit(i64 val) {\n    bool isNegative = val < 0;\n    if (isNegative) val = -val;\n    i64 adjustment = 0;\n    i64 original = val;\n    while (val > 0) {\n        adjustment = adjustment * 10 + (isNegative ? -1 : 1);\n        val /= 10;\n    }\n    adjustment = adjustment * 10 + 1;\n    return isNegative ? original + adjustment : original - adjustment;\n}\n\ni64 getFirstDigit(i64 val) {\n    if (val < 0) val = -val;\n    while (val >= 10) {\n        val /= 10;\n    }\n    return val;\n}\n\ni64 removeLastDigit(i64 val) {\n    if (val < 0) val = -val;\n    vector<int> digits;\n    while (val >= 10) {\n        digits.push_back(val % 10);\n        val /= 10;\n    }\n    i64 res = 0;\n    for (int i = digits.size() - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        res = res * 10 + digits[i];\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nunordered_map<i64, i64> cache;\n\ni64 compute(i64 val) {\n    if (val <= 11) return min(13 - val, val);\n    if (cache.count(val)) return cache[val];\n    i64 n = 0, threshold = 1;\n    while (threshold < val) {\n        threshold *= 10;\n        threshold += 1;\n        ++n;\n    }\n    if (val * 2 >= threshold) {\n        i64 option1 = compute(threshold - val) + n + 1;\n        i64 base = threshold / 10;\n        i64 option2 = (val / base) * n + compute(val % base);\n        return cache[val] = min(option1, option2);\n    }\n    i64 base = threshold / 10;\n    return cache[val] = (val / base) * n + compute(val % base);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    i64 input;\n    cin >> input;\n    cout << compute(input) << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\n\ndef digit_count(val):\n    if val == 0:\n        return 1\n    if val < 0:\n        val = -val\n    cnt = 0\n    while val > 0:\n        cnt += 1\n        val //= 10\n    return cnt\n\ndef increment_each_digit(val):\n    digits = []\n    is_negative = val < 0\n    if is_negative:\n        val = -val\n    while val > 0:\n        d = val % 10\n        digits.append(d - (-1 if is_negative else 1))\n        val //= 10\n    res = 0\n    for i in range(len(digits) - 1, -1, -1):\n        res = res * 10 + digits[i]\n    return -res if is_negative else res\n\ndef decrement_each_digit(val):\n    is_negative = val < 0\n    if is_negative:\n        val = -val\n    adjustment = 0\n    while val > 0:\n        adjustment = adjustment * 10 + (1 if is_negative else -1)\n        val //= 10\n    adjustment = adjustment * 10 + 1\n    return val + adjustment if is_negative else val - adjustment\n\ndef get_first_digit(val):\n    if val < 0:\n        val = -val\n    while val >= 10:\n        val //= 10\n    return val\n\ndef remove_last_digit(val):\n    if val < 0:\n        val = -val\n    digits = []\n    while val >= 10:\n        digits.append(val % 10)\n        val //= 10\n    res = 0\n    for i in range(len(digits) - 1, -1, -1):\n        res = res * 10 + digits[i]\n    return res\n\ncache = {}\n\ndef compute(val):\n    if val <= 11:\n        return min(13 - val, val)\n    if val in cache:\n        return cache[val]\n    n = 0\n    threshold = 1\n    while threshold < val:\n        threshold = threshold * 10 + 1\n        n += 1\n    if val * 2 >= threshold:\n        option1 = compute(threshold - val) + n + 1\n        base = threshold // 10\n        option2 = (val // base) * n + compute(val % base)\n        cache[val] = min(option1, option2)\n        return cache[val]\n    base = threshold // 10\n    cache[val] = (val // base) * n + compute(val % base)\n    return cache[val]\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    input_val = int(input_data[0])\n    print(compute(input_val))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00018380382971372455, -9.536738616588991e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.6032654047012329, -0.00033790123416110873, -0.007609192747622728, -0.2018430531024933, -0.5777001976966858, -3.5762781180892